WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.658
A brand-new browser

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.873
built from scratch

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.041
enters alpha

00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:05.733
Ladybird is an

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:06.889
independent web browser

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.750
built from scratch

00:00:07.927 --> 00:00:08.622
and it has

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:09.507
now entered alpha

00:00:09.318 --> 00:00:09.966
testing

00:00:10.097 --> 00:00:10.945
the stage where

00:00:10.757 --> 00:00:11.606
a browser is

00:00:11.417 --> 00:00:12.455
complete enough for

00:00:12.266 --> 00:00:13.221
early users to

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:13.669
try

00:00:14.206 --> 00:00:15.361
Built from scratch

00:00:15.303 --> 00:00:16.210
means the team

00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:16.871
wrote the browser

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:17.472
themselves

00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:18.533
rather than building

00:00:18.345 --> 00:00:19.135
on top of

00:00:18.947 --> 00:00:20.255
another browser's code

00:00:20.774 --> 00:00:21.929
Alpha testing is

00:00:21.741 --> 00:00:22.472
the moment a

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:23.344
project like this

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.052
stops being a

00:00:23.864 --> 00:00:25.207
demo and starts

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:26.245
being something people

00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:27.153
can actually use

00:00:26.977 --> 00:00:27.778
every day

00:00:28.302 --> 00:00:29.316
Full story on

00:00:29.127 --> 00:00:30.023
the dashboard
